BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (hand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (Practitioners also agree on the order of attack. Coryn Janish opens with the mains voltage test and records the value,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (then ground resistance, then earth leakage in normal polarity with the machine on, then chassis leakage with the ground) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (open and closed [kAjv16M8WpI @ 00:00:29]. Biomedical Engineers TV frames the same ladder against IEC 60601,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (AAMI and NFPA 99: protective earth applies to Class I equipment only and should not normally exceed 0.2 ohms,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (earth leakage runs in normal polarity and normal condition, enclosure leakage runs in both polarities and applies to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Class 1 and Class 2, and patient leakage on CF parts is measured per applied part [ko-zuQ3-hHY @ 00:03:49]. Biomed) Tj ET
