BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 596.00 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 573.77 Tm (The first trap is trusting the analyzer before proving it. Better Biomed Channel warns that if the lead is defective, every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 558.55 Tm (other measurement doesn't matter whatsoever. The check is to clip to the 1 ohm stud, select earth resistance, and expect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 543.32 Tm (a reading that stabilizes near 1 ohm. All metals oxidize at the surface layer, so a high reading means rotating the clamp) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 528.10 Tm (to break through [HBf8beE8tGc @ 00:00:49]. The current side gets verified on the 100 microamp stud in enclosure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 512.87 Tm (leakage mode, where the result came in off by 0.5 of a microamp [HBf8beE8tGc @ 00:01:39]. AbishkarTECH shows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 497.65 Tm (what a bad supply looks like on screen: a no-ground fault. Live-to-neutral read a correct 225, but live-to-earth read 53) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 482.42 Tm (when it should have matched, and neutral-to-earth read 32 against an expected figure under five [rqUE2pFiqUI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 467.20 Tm (00:00:44]. That same ground fault and a loose connection pushed protective earth to 0.062 against roughly 0.03, even) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 451.97 Tm (after the leads were zeroed [rqUE2pFiqUI @ 00:02:03]. Better Biomed Channel zeros leads on the SA 2600 because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 436.75 Tm (leads carry inherent resistance, then flexes the cord at both ends during the ground read [6JXtlTgXvKo @ 00:01:40].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 421.52 Tm (Skipping lead and supply verification puts every downstream pass or fail in doubt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 406.30 Tm (Power faults burn the most bench time when the tech grabs the obvious fix. Better Biomed Channel's beginner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 391.07 Tm (troubleshooting run says it bluntly: a band-aid fix always comes back, and that includes replacing fuses, because a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.85 Tm (replaced fuse will pop again [7JgSRU2VyXE @ 00:08:14]. The same speaker guarantees that a device that pops a fuse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.62 Tm (has bigger problems, which is why fuses sit last in the no-power workflow [7JgSRU2VyXE @ 00:07:52]. The cheaper) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 345.40 Tm (misses come first. Hospitals often pop circuit breakers, so outlet and cord get checked before the case comes open. On) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.17 Tm (devices that run 100% off the battery, a fully depleted battery can pass for a dead supply [7JgSRU2VyXE @ 00:07:17].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.95 Tm (Current draw also shifts under load. AbishkarTECH read 0.2 A at idle and warns the draw may read higher under load,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 299.72 Tm (so consumption is cross-checked against the manufacturer's rating [rqUE2pFiqUI @ 00:04:56]. Better Biomed Channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 284.50 Tm (sets a 30-second timer on the SA 2600 to give heating elements and motors time to come up before the current read) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 269.27 Tm ([6JXtlTgXvKo @ 00:02:52]. Battery operation is its own trap. Jamie Spragus notes that most safety tests can't run on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 254.05 Tm (battery, even though the ESA700 analyzer itself runs about two hours on one [x772T1-4M-Q @ 00:39:28].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 238.82 Tm (Out-of-tolerance readings carry clinical and money stakes. ATHEENAPANDIAN BIOMEDICAL INDUSTRY warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 223.60 Tm (that miscalibration causes serious harm because doctors trust the display, which can lead to unnecessary ICU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 208.37 Tm (admissions [-ZSbkKuzbMc @ 00:08:18]. The rule is that no approximation is given when calibrating a device) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 193.15 Tm ([-ZSbkKuzbMc @ 00:30:52]. An oxygen concentrator in the same demo dropped to 41% under poor ventilation, well) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 177.92 Tm (below the 73% red-alarm line. The yellow threshold was stated as 85% in one pass and 82% in another [-ZSbkKuzbMc) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 162.70 Tm (@ 01:25:02]. Isiah's FT10 procedure is unforgiving. Persistent alarms at boot halt testing, and RF output at 30, 100 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 147.47 Tm (300 W must stay within 10% of the set point. If a reading falls outside tolerance, recalibration or service intervention is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 132.25 Tm (required [bLqvmql3QHs @ 00:05:42]. Tooling has its own ceilings. Spragus's 1QA Basic plan allows only 5) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 117.02 Tm (procedures while Complete is unlimited, and every procedure carries a single standard [x772T1-4M-Q @ 00:34:15].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 101.80 Tm (The credential path has a fee trap too. On the online-proctored CABT, leaving the area means termination and forfeited) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 86.57 Tm (fees, and most other violations get one warning before termination [B0yNPMYGzqM @ 00:14:35].) Tj ET
