BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 464.87 Tm (last two consultant-led submissions passed on the first try [gGje01O9B44 @ 00:13:09]. Qualio's numbers are lower but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 449.65 Tm (still brutal, with 30% of submissions last year not even accepted for initial review [1GKnWm8UYVk @ 00:54:07].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.42 Tm (Inside eSTAR the failure points shift but do not vanish. Packard sees 'so many RTAs just because companies don't have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.20 Tm (a level of concern documentation in the package,' and he flags missing wireless coexistence testing as another common) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 403.97 Tm (trigger [b1Ejw4mhVFU @ 00:15:58]. The small stuff bites too. In the Part I workshop, an inconsistent device name) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 388.75 Tm (across headers triggers RTA, a condom was rejected over the 'patient contacting' field, and a wrong Rx/OTC checkbox) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 373.52 Tm (costs about $5k and another 90 days.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.30 Tm (Dave Saunders describes a company that got 48 hours to produce a 40,000-page DHF, hand-delivered it, and still failed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.07 Tm (clearance. His yardstick is that a 510\(k\) runs 200 to 500 pages sitting on a DHF of roughly 10,000 [6w27HXwMbmU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 327.85 Tm (@ 00:32:12]. He warns 'you cannot create this documentation retroactively,' and says a change log where every change) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 312.62 Tm (is approved 'suggests a rubber stamp process' [6w27HXwMbmU @ 00:36:12]. Sagar Tipne's remediation interview) Tj ET
