BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every practitioner who works the recall side starts from the same definition. Amanda Johnston of Gardner Law frames) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (a recall as the removal or correction of violative product, explicitly excluding market withdrawals and stock recovery) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm ([aYQu_0ujhyU @ 00:07:25]. Aaron Snyder compresses Part 806 into five words, 'report field actions to fda,' and states) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (that all Class 1 and Class 2 recalls must be reported within 10 days of initiating the recall [8Pgfw2y5xe0 @ 00:01:52].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Steve Needelman, 34 years at FDA before joining King & Spalding, sharpens the trigger: the 10 business days run from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (the decision to act, not from the date the customer letter goes out [nJblY5CRIVY @ 00:04:43]. Jeff Kasof repeats the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (number flatly: the deadline for issuing the report is 10 working days [1kYC2rBfPPA @ 00:41:45]. The classes line up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (the same way across speakers: Class 1 is highest risk, Class 2 moderate, Class 3 lowest, and FDA, not the firm, assigns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (the final class, although a company can propose one through its health hazard evaluation. Johnston adds that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (reportability is decided on the risk-to-health definition rather than the class definitions, and that unreported corrections) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (and removals still require kept records. For anyone moving used equipment, that vocabulary is the filter for reading) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (every recall entry attached to a unit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (The second point of agreement is that almost nothing here is forced, and that hiding a recall is the expensive move.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Needelman says FDA's mandatory recall authority has existed since 1990 and been used fewer than 10 times, putting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (voluntary recalls at '99.999%' [nJblY5CRIVY @ 00:05:39]; Johnston lands in the 'high 90%' range. Treomark warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (against misreading that word: 'voluntary' describes how a recall began, not how severe it is, and not every unit is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (physically returned [GoXd4_jxKBg @ 00:00:16]. Tim Phillips, who spent 12 years as an FDA investigator and 20 as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (compliance officer, is blunt that recalls cannot be disguised as a 'technical bulletin' and that there are no quiet recalls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm ([aYQu_0ujhyU @ 00:34:48]. Needelman backs that with a Medrad warning letter as his silent-recall example and a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (bulb hypothetical: failures at 22 to 23 months are not a recall, failures at 8 to 9 months are, and a depleted backup) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (battery is a recall [nJblY5CRIVY @ 00:51:13]. David Graham, a litigator with 35-plus years, explains why it matters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (downstream: a recall makes information public, and an opaque one turns a 'bad device case' into a 'bad company case.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (Graham's working assumption is that every document goes public eventually.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (On the data side, the consensus is that MAUDE is free, public, and badly limited, and that operators should use it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (anyway. Abby Smart, an epidemiologist at Ofstead Insights, dates the database to 1991 and notes it is searchable for 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (years of reports [a-scTl1C2PA @ 00:01:12]; Dr. Ibrahim Alawad gives the same 1991 start and 10-year window, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (Dr. Hashem stresses that no hospital data is needed because the database is free and public. Three speakers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (independently hit the same wall when pulling large device histories: output is capped at 500 records per search. Alawad) Tj ET
