BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.77 Tm (The most expensive mistake the FDA veterans describe is timing, and the second is disguise. Phillips says a late 806) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.55 Tm (report invites a 483 or a warning letter scaled to how late it was, and a firm that hoped nobody would notice is still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.32 Tm (exposed when an investigator finds it months later [aYQu_0ujhyU @ 00:22:33]. They also flag the camouflage moves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 352.10 Tm (FDA sees through: a recall dressed up as a technical bulletin, or a quiet recall [aYQu_0ujhyU @ 00:34:48]. Needelman) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.87 Tm (draws the silent-recall line with a bulb hypothetical: lamps failing at 22 to 23 months are not a recall, lamps failing at 8) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.65 Tm (to 9 months are, and a depleted backup battery is a recall too; they cite a Medrad warning letter as the live example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.42 Tm ([nJblY5CRIVY @ 00:51:13]. Their fix for the clock is blunt: 80% of the information on time beats 100% late, amend) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 291.20 Tm (later, and promptly reporting in those 10 days is critical [nJblY5CRIVY @ 00:52:35]. The trap on the other side is an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.97 Tm (806 report stuffed with placeholder entries, which they say has no value at all. Phillips adds that vague recall letters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.75 Tm (raise red flags, and that asking FDA what you should do is not a plan.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.52 Tm (MAUDE punishes anyone who reads it at face value. The Health Watch USA pharmacology researcher ran roughly 7.5) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.30 Tm (million events from 1997 to 2018 through custom software and found manufacturers filed 96.6% of reports, possibly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.07 Tm (driven by warranty claims and lawsuits, while physicians filed directly only 0.49% and facilities 1.3% despite) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.85 Tm (mandatory reporting [yKomHc_DWtw @ 00:05:20]. The same study hit Johnson & Johnson logged under multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.62 Tm (name variants, common duplicates, and a cobalt toxicity pull of 14,714 records where only 4% listed lab levels) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.40 Tm ([yKomHc_DWtw @ 00:07:05]. Smart warns that narratives can be empty and get filled in later, that reports arrive late) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.17 Tm (and underreported, and that FDA itself says MAUDE cannot assess prevalence [a-scTl1C2PA @ 00:09:23]. Bernstein) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.95 Tm (adds that clinical sites and manufacturers each file narratives on the same problem, very ill patients confound causation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.72 Tm (and a record is not causation until it is cross-checked against manufacturer claims, patient records and FDA findings) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 108.50 Tm ([xbxXTRwdVRs @ 00:30:15]. Alawad's zero-result fix is to widen dates, drop brand and event type, and try every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 93.27 Tm (manufacturer name variant, as with Rosh versus Rocher. Gene Parunak still calls a cursory keyword look at similar) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 78.05 Tm (devices well worth your time.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8 Tf 270.00 30 Td (Page 124 of 198) Tj ET
