BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (by ANSI, and that any MLSO course must be Board of Laser Safety approved if the student ever wants certification) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm ([4yS9pDHEcIs @ 00:22:50]. Patty Owens hammers the same line on TechNation TV: the Board 'will not accept other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (types of courses' from pop-up training companies, which is why their own two-day class went through BLS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (accreditation [kBlmK6r6MgU @ 00:47:38]. The opposite playbook comes from the Laser Safety Certification portal,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (which sells fully online courses where staff get 'certified in about an hour,' print the certificate instantly, and are pitched) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (as 100% OSHA compliant across class 1 to class 4 lasers [QnVjairPvRk @ 00:00:54]. Ohio Optometric sits between) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (the two, arguing that a 32-hour course mixing lectures, videos and hands-on simulations is 'more than sufficient' to put) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (YAG capsulotomy and SLT into optometry offices as in-office procedures [3pHyNlFBLO0 @ 00:02:12]. For an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (operator staffing a laser service line, a one-hour printed certificate, a two-day BLS-approved course and a 32-hour) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (clinical course are three very different pieces of paper, and only the BLS-approved route feeds the CLSO or CMLSO) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (application after a year of hands-on LSO duty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (On the treatment floor, the disagreements are about wavelength, cooling and speed. Dr. Azi of Skin By Dr. Azi calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (the 755 nm alexandrite 'the most potent' option, ideal for very white skin and dark hair, but also the most uncomfortable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (and the slowest, while the 1064 nm YAG is the safer pick for darker skin because it bypasses surface melanin and goes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (more directly to the hair root [lY2Cys5Df0c @ 00:02:57]. The same dermatologist goes the other way for heavy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (growth, telling patients, particularly men, to start on IPL or BBL to cut hair density at roughly half the treatment time,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (then switch to the more potent laser [lY2Cys5Df0c @ 00:06:21]. Marianne Urban, interviewed by Laser Coach, runs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (both a Candela GentleMax Pro and a Cynosure Elite MPX with the same 755 and 1064 wavelengths and says the real) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (difference is cooling: cryogen spray on the Candela versus Zimmer cold air on the Cynosure, with clients sometimes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (preferring one over the other [IOSA5f1D4nI @ 00:00:13]. Speed is the last fault line. At a 24 mm spot and 2 Hz, full) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (legs take about 45 minutes, yet that clinic refuses to 'just fly through the treatments' for speed only and builds in breaks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (to check tolerance and skin response [2a1E_LFIa6I @ 00:00:32].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (Even the safety veterans split on how rigid the program must be. Dennis says the LSO does not have to run every case:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (in a small dental office the LSO may be the person activating the laser, but at Emory, with 200 lasers on the university) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (side and 50 or 60 outpatient, the job only worked through deputy LSOs, site contacts and a dedicated laser safety) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (specialist in each room [4yS9pDHEcIs @ 00:54:30]. On TechNation TV, Dennis gives biomedical engineers the edge) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (because they already know the equipment, and, recalling a 200-laser program, says 'There is no way I could wear the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (hat as a manager and do that too' [kBlmK6r6MgU @ 00:13:16]. Medical surveillance is a full reversal: blanket) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (pre-employment and exit eye exams have given way to surveillance limited to staff with known risk, and Owens notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (baseline exams 'have proven not to be useful' in medical legal litigation, while post-incident exams are what matter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm ([kBlmK6r6MgU @ 00:34:55]. Eyewear around fibers is the slipperiest call. Dennis says waiving goggles puts the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (liability on the LSO because fibers break, and the only waiver they have seen is a rigid articulating arm attached to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (laparoscope, written into policy with the nominal hazard zone documented [4yS9pDHEcIs @ 00:56:55].) Tj ET
BT /F0 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (Competing playbooks practitioners run on the same laser decisions) Tj ET
